    "review": "The Dead hit their stride at the West Palm Beach Auditorium on September 11, 1982.  From the opening “New Minglewood Blues” through a tight first set that builds into an inspired “Let It Grow,” the band is locked in, with Jerry’s guitar soaring and Brent’s keyboards adding a fiery edge.  The second set erupts with one of the era’s most memorable segues – a blistering Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain that drives the whole night forward, while Phil’s bass underpins every twist with smooth, fast‑grooving lines.  Terrapin Station rolls out with layered drumming from Mickey and Bill, leading into an expansive “Truckin’” > “Stella Blue” stretch that feels both relaxed and explosive.  Highlights like Dupree’s Diamond Blues, Lost Sailor → Saint of Circumstance, and a soulful encore of “It’s All Over Now Baby Blue” round out a show that still feels fresh and vibrant decades later.",
